    "updated_at": "2022-05-17T07:27:46Z",
    "body": "> @noamr may have thoughts on the best architecture here. I think the main question is, do we pass other algorithms (whether in this spec or other specs) the raw times, and rely on them to relativize/coarsen/etc.? Or do we pass them appropriate relative times?\r\n\r\nWe usually try to relativize and coarsen as soon as we can. Where we pass around the `unsafe shared current time` is in cases where e.g. we don't have a clear `global object` yet (e.g. when processing the event loop).\r\n\r\nThe right architecture here should be that step 13 in the processing model should relativize and coarsen `now` based on document's relevant global object. It's an easy fix.\r\n",
